---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';

const lastUpdated = 'August 11, 2026';
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Security &amp; Vulnerability Disclosure | Michael LaPlante"
  description="Vulnerability disclosure policy for michaellaplante.com — scope, how to report a security issue, good-faith safe harbor, and how this site is secured."
>
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <meta name="author" content="Michael LaPlante">
    <link rel="preload" href="/fonts/poppins/poppins-400.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin>
    <link rel="preload" href="/fonts/poppins/poppins-700.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin>
    <link rel="stylesheet" type="text/css" href="/css/fonts.css">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/bootstrap.min.css">
    <link rel="stylesheet" type="text/css" href="/css/style.css">
  </Fragment>

  <!-- Skip to Content Link for Accessibility -->
  <a href="#main-content" class="skip-to-content">Skip to main content</a>

  <!--========================================
    Menu
  =========================================-->
  <nav class="top-nav" aria-label="Main navigation">
    <div class="container">

      <button type="button" class="menu-btn" aria-label="Toggle menu" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="site-menu">
        <span class="lines">
          <span class="l1"></span>
          <span class="l2"></span>
          <span class="l3"></span>
        </span>
      </button>

      <button class="dark-mode-toggle" aria-label="Toggle dark mode" title="Toggle dark mode">
        <span class="sun-icon">☀️</span>
        <span class="moon-icon">🌙</span>
      </button>

      <div class="menu" id="site-menu">
        <ul>
          <li><a href="/">Home</a></li>
          <li><a href="/services/">Services</a></li>
          <li><a href="/blog/">Blog</a></li>
          <li><a href="/uses/">Uses</a></li>
          <li><a href="/resume/">Resume</a></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </nav>

  <!--========================================
    Main Content
  =========================================-->
  <main id="main-content">

  <section class="section" id="security-header" style="padding-top: 120px;">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-header" data-aos="fade-up">
        <h1 style='font-size: 18px; font-weight: 700; font-family: "Roboto Mono", monospace; text-transform: lowercase; letter-spacing: 2px; position: relative; display: inline-block;'>security</h1>
      </div>
      <p data-aos="fade-up" class="updated">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="security-body">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="legal" data-aos="fade-up">

        <p>
          This page is the vulnerability disclosure policy for
          <strong>michaellaplante.com</strong>, the personal portfolio and blog
          of Michael LaPlante. Security work is my day job, and I welcome
          good-faith reports about this site. To set expectations up front:
          this is a solo-run personal website, and this is
          <strong>not a paid bug bounty program</strong> — there are no
          monetary rewards, but I will gladly credit you (with your
          permission) for a valid finding.
        </p>

        <h2>Scope</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>michaellaplante.com</strong> — the site itself, including the contact form API.</li>
          <li><strong><a href="https://github.com/mlaplante/resumesite" target="_blank" rel="noopener">github.com/mlaplante/resumesite</a></strong> — the public source repository for this site, including its build and deployment workflows.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>How to report</h2>
        <p>
          Please report security issues through the
          <a href="/#contact">contact form</a> — it's the primary channel and
          reaches me directly. This policy is also referenced from the site's
          <a href="/.well-known/security.txt">security.txt</a>. For
          non-sensitive issues in the source code, a GitHub issue on the
          repository works too.
        </p>

        <h2>What to include</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>A description of the issue and where you found it (URL, endpoint, or file/commit in the repository).</li>
          <li>Steps to reproduce, or a proof of concept.</li>
          <li>The impact as you understand it — what could an attacker actually do?</li>
          <li>Any relevant environment details (browser, tooling), and how you'd like to be credited, if at all.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>What to expect</h2>
        <p>
          I'll acknowledge your report within a few business days, keep you
          posted on what I find, and let you know when the issue is fixed.
          This site is run by one person in his spare time, so complex issues
          may take longer to resolve — but I take reports seriously and won't
          leave you hanging.
        </p>

        <h2>Safe harbor</h2>
        <p>
          I authorize good-faith security research against the scope above,
          and I consider it authorized under this policy. If you make a
          good-faith effort to follow this policy:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>I will not pursue or support legal action against you for your research, including accidental, good-faith violations of this policy.</li>
          <li>If you encounter personal data (for example, someone else's contact-form submission), stop, don't save or share it, and report what you found — that's a normal part of good-faith research, not a violation.</li>
          <li>If you're ever unsure whether something is in scope or allowed, ask first via the <a href="/#contact">contact form</a>.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Out of scope</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Denial of service, volumetric, or load testing of any kind.</li>
          <li>Spam, phishing, or social engineering of me or anyone else.</li>
          <li>Physical attacks against people, property, or infrastructure.</li>
          <li>Automated scanner output without a demonstrated, exploitable impact (e.g., version banners, or missing-header reports on pages where the header isn't applicable).</li>
          <li>Third-party services this site relies on but doesn't control: Cal.com (scheduling), Cloudflare Turnstile, ForwardEmail, and the Netlify-hosted Umami analytics instance. Report issues in those platforms to their own security programs.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>How this site is secured</h2>
        <p>
          In the spirit of transparency — and because the
          <a href="https://github.com/mlaplante/resumesite" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source is public</a>
          anyway — here's a summary of the current security posture:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Strict security headers.</strong> Every page ships a
            Content-Security-Policy whose <code>script-src</code> allows no
            <code>'unsafe-inline'</code> — scripts load only from this origin
            and a short allowlist of named services. HSTS is set for one year
            with <code>includeSubDomains</code> and <code>preload</code>, and
            framing is blocked entirely (<code>frame-ancestors 'none'</code>
            plus <code>X-Frame-Options: DENY</code>).
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Hardened contact form.</strong> The contact API enforces
            same-origin requests, verifies a Cloudflare Turnstile challenge
            that fails closed if verification can't complete, rate-limits
            attempts per IP, caps payload sizes, strips control characters to
            prevent email-header injection, and purges stored submissions
            after 90 days.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Supply-chain controls in CI.</strong> All GitHub Actions
            are pinned to full commit SHAs, CodeQL and gitleaks scans run on
            the repository, workflow files are linted with zizmor, and
            Dependabot checks dependencies weekly.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          None of this makes the site invulnerable — that's what this policy
          is for. If you spot a gap, I'd like to hear about it.
        </p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Questions about this policy? Reach out through the
          <a href="/#contact">contact form</a>.
        </p>

      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  </main>

  <!--========================================
    Footer
  =========================================-->
  <footer>
    <div class="container">
      <p class="copyright" data-aos="fade-up">
        Copyright &copy; LaPlante Web Development 2006-<span id="copyright-year"></span>.
        <a href="/privacy/">Privacy</a>
        <a href="/security/">Security</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </footer>

  <!--========================================
    JavaScript Files
  =========================================-->
  <script is:inline defer src="/js/script.js"></script>
</SiteLayout>

<style>
  .updated {
    font-family: 'Roboto Mono', monospace;
    font-size: 13px;
    color: #6b7280;
    letter-spacing: 0.5px;
  }

  .legal {
    max-width: 760px;
  }

  .legal p,
  .legal li {
    font-family: 'Poppins', sans-serif;
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.8;
    color: #374151;
  }

  .legal p {
    margin-bottom: 18px;
  }

  .legal h2 {
    font-family: 'Poppins', sans-serif;
    font-size: 20px;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: #111827;
    margin: 36px 0 12px;
  }

  .legal ul {
    margin: 0 0 18px;
    padding-left: 22px;
  }

  .legal li {
    margin-bottom: 10px;
  }

  .legal a {
    color: #2980b9;
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  .legal a:hover {
    opacity: 0.7;
  }

  .legal code {
    font-family: 'Roboto Mono', monospace;
    font-size: 14px;
  }

  :global([data-theme='dark']) .updated { color: #94a3b8; }
  :global([data-theme='dark']) .legal p,
  :global([data-theme='dark']) .legal li { color: #cbd5e1; }
  :global([data-theme='dark']) .legal h2 { color: #f1f5f9; }
  :global([data-theme='dark']) .legal a { color: #60a5fa; }

  :global(body.dark-mode) .updated { color: #94a3b8; }
  :global(body.dark-mode) .legal p,
  :global(body.dark-mode) .legal li { color: #cbd5e1; }
  :global(body.dark-mode) .legal h2 { color: #f1f5f9; }
  :global(body.dark-mode) .legal a { color: #60a5fa; }
</style>
